## 10. Measurement

- Recheck each page at 14 and 28 days using same-length GSC windows. Compare CTR, clicks, impressions, and position against the baseline above.
- Leave the pages ranked 26–50 by click gap untouched as a control. If their CTR moves the same way, the lift did not come from the meta changes.
- Halloween and fall pages will drop in November regardless. Judge them on CTR at the same position, not on raw clicks.
- Expect feature-suspected pages to move least.

## 11. Hard limits

- Never fabricate SERP data, GSC data, or competitor titles.
- One page at a time. Never present several pages together.
- Keep every message to the section 5 format.
- Make only user-approved changes.
